How much does it cost.

1543
01:06:18,658 --> 01:06:19,964
- I'm not done yet.

1544
01:06:19,964 --> 01:06:22,820
Gasp in horror at the
largely ironic midway

1545
01:06:22,820 --> 01:06:27,518
and squeal with delight at
the antics of Nate the Clown.

1546
01:06:27,518 --> 01:06:28,890
- Hey that's me.

1547
01:06:28,890 --> 01:06:32,057
(laughs like a clown)

1548
01:06:33,429 --> 01:06:35,930
- Okay, okay, you've sold me.

1549
01:06:35,930 --> 01:06:37,434
How much?

1550
01:06:37,434 --> 01:06:40,767
- Only 25 cents, that's right a quarter.

1551
01:06:41,847 --> 01:06:45,106
Two bits, five nickels, one
quarter of a green back.

1552
01:06:45,106 --> 01:06:48,158
- Well I've got a handful of quarters.

1553
01:06:48,158 --> 01:06:49,029
You guys in?

1554
01:06:49,029 --> 01:06:49,862
- You bet.

1555
01:06:49,862 --> 01:06:50,695
- I want to see the ironic midway.

1556
01:06:50,695 --> 01:06:52,417
- Here ya go, pallie.

1557
01:06:52,417 --> 01:06:53,639
(screams)

1558
01:06:53,639 --> 01:06:56,580
- Oh horrors, the curse
of the circus is upon us.

1559
01:06:56,580 --> 01:06:58,752
Giant stones fall from the sky.

1560
01:06:58,752 --> 01:07:00,575
And our clown is dead.

1561
01:07:00,575 --> 01:07:01,870
(crying)

1562
01:07:01,870 --> 01:07:03,510
- [Voiceover] Ah, the
microbes are on the loose.

1563
01:07:03,510 --> 01:07:05,437
The ameobas are on the rampage.

1564
01:07:05,437 --> 01:07:06,270
Run!

1565
01:07:08,525 --> 01:07:09,358
- Ow, sorry.

1566
01:07:09,358 --> 01:07:10,814
I was just tossing one on and

1567
01:07:10,814 --> 01:07:11,734
Oh!

1568
01:07:11,734 --> 01:07:12,917
- Here comes another.

1569
01:07:12,917 --> 01:07:14,669
The circus is destroyed.

1570
01:07:14,669 --> 01:07:16,016
(sighs)

1571
01:07:16,016 --> 01:07:18,175
- Maybe we should go to the zoo instead.

1572
01:07:18,175 --> 01:07:19,089
- That's a good idea.

1573
01:07:19,089 --> 01:07:20,531
We'll be right back.

1574
01:07:20,531 --> 01:07:21,922
- Clown killer.

1575
01:07:21,922 --> 01:07:22,755
- Maybe.

1576
01:07:30,580 --> 01:07:34,392
- [Crow] Geez, did ya
see that clown blood?

1577
01:07:34,392 --> 01:07:36,677
- Man your stations.

1578
01:07:36,677 --> 01:07:39,903
- [Servo] I don't think
the sanctions are working.

1579
01:07:39,903 --> 01:07:42,153
- Get your lines ready sir.

1580
01:07:43,431 --> 01:07:45,531
- Open the valves.

1581
01:07:45,531 --> 01:07:49,698
- [Crow] Ah, they're gonna get
it drunk on woodpecker cider.

1582
01:07:51,877 --> 01:07:54,300
♫ Downtown ♫

1583
01:07:54,300 --> 01:07:57,203
- [Voiceover] Come on hop to it.

1584
01:07:57,203 --> 01:08:01,370
- [Servo] The kales navy
only battle the creature.

1585
01:08:08,690 --> 01:08:11,940
- [Crow] Come on it's the 5:15 monster.

1586
01:08:14,382 --> 01:08:15,276
- Be ready.

1587
01:08:15,276 --> 01:08:17,066
Let's get behind those sandbags.

1588
01:08:17,066 --> 01:08:20,046
- [Mike] This feels good,
squishing the mud between my toes.

1589
01:08:20,046 --> 01:08:21,172
- Fire.

1590
01:08:21,172 --> 01:08:22,035
- [Servo] Got him.

1591
01:08:22,035 --> 01:08:22,868
He's dead.

1592
01:08:22,868 --> 01:08:23,701
It's over.

1593
01:08:23,701 --> 01:08:24,876
- [Mike] Good, let's go.

1594
01:08:24,876 --> 01:08:26,428
- [Crow] This is a fine welcome.

1595
01:08:26,428 --> 01:08:30,454
They treated Jerry Lee
Lewis better than this.

1596
01:08:30,454 --> 01:08:32,454
- [Mike] Bullocks Gorgo.

1597
01:08:35,745 --> 01:08:37,931
(laughing)

1598
01:08:37,931 --> 01:08:42,098
- [Crow] Now that just
seemed completely avoidable.

1599
01:08:46,970 --> 01:08:49,596
- Get me army headquarters.

1600
01:08:49,596 --> 01:08:51,261
- Atomic weapons are out of the question.

1601
01:08:51,261 --> 01:08:52,273
(mumbling)

1602
01:08:52,273 --> 01:08:53,175
- [Servo] Wacko.

1603
01:08:53,175 --> 01:08:54,322
- Tanks?

1604
01:08:54,322 --> 01:08:55,337
Of course.

1605
01:08:55,337 --> 01:08:57,693
- [Mike] Come on let's do something easy

1606
01:08:57,693 --> 01:09:00,860
like put down some Arabs or something.

1607
01:09:04,406 --> 01:09:05,475
- [Servo] Those things are great.

1608
01:09:05,475 --> 01:09:07,456
They're built like Volvos.

1609
01:09:07,456 --> 01:09:08,289
- Attention.

1610
01:09:08,289 --> 01:09:10,117
This is a special bulletin.

1611
01:09:10,117 --> 01:09:13,064
Civil defense authorities have
declared a state of emergency

1612
01:09:13,064 --> 01:09:16,740
for all London areas within
three miles of the River Tims.

1613
01:09:16,740 --> 01:09:18,444
- [Crow] Ah, he'll
probably be sated on people

1614
01:09:18,444 --> 01:09:20,527
from the suburbs by then.

1615
01:09:25,215 --> 01:09:28,715
- [Servo] There's a sale on bumber shoots.

1616
01:09:30,779 --> 01:09:32,860
- [Crow] See it's not so bad.

1617
01:09:32,860 --> 01:09:34,147
Keep your chin up.

1618
01:09:34,147 --> 01:09:35,397
Stiff up a lip.

1619
01:09:36,330 --> 01:09:38,588
- [Voiceover] The streets
must be kept clear

1620
01:09:38,588 --> 01:09:41,171
for military defense personnel.

1621
01:09:42,189 --> 01:09:44,772
- [Mike] And good humor trucks.

1622
01:09:46,502 --> 01:09:47,775
- [Servo] Ah the queen mama's brought out

1623
01:09:47,775 --> 01:09:49,607
to fight the beast.

1624
01:09:49,607 --> 01:09:50,891
Hello.

1625
01:09:50,891 --> 01:09:51,724
Hello.

1626
01:09:57,839 --> 01:10:00,006
(yelling)

1627
01:10:03,368 --> 01:10:05,341
- [Servo] Yes sir.

1628
01:10:05,341 --> 01:10:06,733
- [Crow] Being in the British is a sench.

1629
01:10:06,733 --> 01:10:10,445
You just hold a rifle,
run around, and look busy.

1630
01:10:10,445 --> 01:10:11,381
- [Voiceover] Get off the street.

1631
01:10:11,381 --> 01:10:12,651
- [Crow] Okay.

1632
01:10:12,651 --> 01:10:15,275
- [Mike] No, no he's talking to guys.

1633
01:10:15,275 --> 01:10:19,442
- [Voiceover] Get off the
streets and go to your homes.

1634
01:10:20,425 --> 01:10:24,592
- [Mike] Now tanks are brought
in to roll over the doll.

1635
01:10:27,580 --> 01:10:28,675
- [Crow] Yeah this is
the same thing they do

1636
01:10:28,675 --> 01:10:31,062
when Oliver Reid's in town.

1637
01:10:31,062 --> 01:10:33,312
(laughing)

1638
01:10:35,236 --> 01:10:39,100
- [Servo] Can't believe
we all missed the bus.

1639
01:10:39,100 --> 01:10:40,147
- [Voiceover] Up right there.

1640
01:10:40,147 --> 01:10:40,980
Move in, move in.

1641
01:10:40,980 --> 01:10:42,903
Take your positions.

1642
01:10:42,903 --> 01:10:44,403
Parting positions.

1643
01:10:47,824 --> 01:10:50,756
- It's advancing up river
directly towards us.

1644
01:10:50,756 --> 01:10:51,750
- [Crow] Stay here and get killed?

1645
01:10:51,750 --> 01:10:52,583
Yes sir.

1646
01:10:52,583 --> 01:10:54,004
- Very good, sir.

1647
01:10:54,004 --> 01:10:55,738
- [Servo] A woman.

1648
01:10:55,738 --> 01:10:57,123
- Although the army
indicates full confidence,

1649
01:10:57,123 --> 01:10:59,812
they report growing
casualties among their forces.

1650
01:10:59,812 --> 01:11:00,939
We are told that Donning Street

1651
01:11:00,939 --> 01:11:03,330
is in constant communication
with other world capitals,

1652
01:11:03,330 --> 01:11:04,523
but great concern is expressed.

1653
01:11:04,523 --> 01:11:08,380
- [Mike] Though I detected
a snicker in their voice.

1654
01:11:08,380 --> 01:11:09,213
- Call headquarters.

1655
01:11:09,213 --> 01:11:10,630
Shoot the flares.

1656
01:11:12,455 --> 01:11:13,661
Open side fire.

1657
01:11:13,661 --> 01:11:14,494
Standby.

1658
01:11:15,907 --> 01:11:17,889
Commence fire.

1659
01:11:17,889 --> 01:11:21,139
- [Crow] Hey, wait I don't have my gun.

1660
01:11:27,120 --> 01:11:31,287
- [Mike] You're the ones who
sold me my anti-missile armor.

1661
01:11:35,407 --> 01:11:39,987
- [Crow] Ah this is really
cleaning my pores, thank you.

1662
01:11:39,987 --> 01:11:41,281
- [Servo] Now Mike, you're
probably gripped with the urge

1663
01:11:41,281 --> 01:11:43,587
to say London Bridge is
falling down at this point,

1664
01:11:43,587 --> 01:11:44,563
but don't, don't.

1665
01:11:44,563 --> 01:11:47,619
This is actually the Tower Bridge.

1666
01:11:47,619 --> 01:11:49,406
♫ London Bridge is falling down ♫

1667
01:11:49,406 --> 01:11:50,921
- [Servo] Mike what did I just tell you?

1668
01:11:50,921 --> 01:11:51,754
- [Mike] What?

1669
01:11:51,754 --> 01:11:53,087
Oh right, sorry.

1670
01:12:01,608 --> 01:12:03,108
- [Crow] Hi, guys.

1671
01:12:05,573 --> 01:12:06,845
- [Mike] Why that's quite bracing

1672
01:12:06,845 --> 01:12:09,428
getting knocked off the bridge.

1673
01:12:11,748 --> 01:12:13,553
- [Servo] Oh red ants.

1674
01:12:13,553 --> 01:12:14,885
- The bridge is gone.

1675
01:12:14,885 --> 01:12:18,266
One of London's oldest landmarks
smashed like matchwood.

1676
01:12:18,266 --> 01:12:20,721
Nothing can stop this
beast so far, nothing.

1677
01:12:20,721 --> 01:12:22,871
Not even point blank canon fire.

1678
01:12:22,871 --> 01:12:23,704
- [Servo] Not women.

1679
01:12:23,704 --> 01:12:24,537
- The entire bridge?

1680
01:12:24,537 --> 01:12:26,912
Then the power of this thing is fantastic.

1681
01:12:26,912 --> 01:12:30,329
- [Servo] And I'm on half power as it is.

1682
01:12:33,990 --> 01:12:36,046
- [Crow] Hi, I'm Gorgo,

1683
01:12:36,046 --> 01:12:39,027
but I'm not Mormo of
the thousand-faced moon.

1684
01:12:39,027 --> 01:12:41,277
(laughing)

1685
01:12:43,661 --> 01:12:46,478
- [Servo] Maybe Mary Poppins
flies in and kicks his ass.

1686
01:12:46,478 --> 01:12:48,895
- [Mike] That I'd pay to see.

1687
01:12:54,453 --> 01:12:57,870
No he has the power to superimpose rocks.

1688
01:13:02,163 --> 01:13:03,428
- Check the missile units.

1689
01:13:03,428 --> 01:13:04,261
Yes sir.

1690
01:13:10,520 --> 01:13:14,681
- [Crow] Cliff Richards is
opening up the palladium.

1691
01:13:14,681 --> 01:13:15,888
- [Servo] Juggling pins I brought in,

1692
01:13:15,888 --> 01:13:17,671
and the monster's managed to keep five

1693
01:13:17,671 --> 01:13:19,504
up in the air at once.

1694
01:13:21,371 --> 01:13:23,136
- And meanwhile the Russians
slip in the back door,

1695
01:13:23,136 --> 01:13:23,969
take over London,

1696
01:13:23,969 --> 01:13:26,386
and rename it Khrushchevgrad.

1697
01:13:28,128 --> 01:13:30,677
- [Crow] They could fling
really hot curry in his eyes.

1698
01:13:30,677 --> 01:13:33,728
- [Servo] Yeah or spray
him with malt vinegar.

1699
01:13:33,728 --> 01:13:34,810
- Back, back, come back.

1700
01:13:34,810 --> 01:13:36,943
- Yes sir, I will.

1701
01:13:36,943 --> 01:13:37,860
40 degrees.

1702
01:13:41,059 --> 01:13:42,414
- [Crow] Hey it's large Bob.

1703
01:13:42,414 --> 01:13:43,484
- [Mike] It's Big Ben.

1704
01:13:43,484 --> 01:13:45,401
- [Crow] Oh sure, Mike.

1705
01:13:53,098 --> 01:13:56,024
- [Servo] You think it's noticeable.

1706
01:13:56,024 --> 01:13:56,857
- [Mike] Nah.

1707
01:13:56,857 --> 01:13:58,828
- [Servo] Oh boy.

1708
01:13:58,828 --> 01:14:00,245
- [Crow] Big Ben.

1709
01:14:01,141 --> 01:14:04,891
- [Mike] It was running
a little fast anyway.

1710
01:14:11,767 --> 01:14:15,517
- [Crow] Got a few people
caught in my teeth.

1711
01:14:17,683 --> 01:14:18,516
- Come on.

1712
01:14:19,977 --> 01:14:23,136
- [Servo] I want access
to the Law Library.

1713
01:14:23,136 --> 01:14:25,387
- Burned out our connection.

1714
01:14:25,387 --> 01:14:26,703
- [Mike] Here let's check is air pressure.

1715
01:14:26,703 --> 01:14:29,474
Maybe that's the problem.

1716
01:14:29,474 --> 01:14:30,807
- Where's Shawn?

1717
01:14:33,694 --> 01:14:34,825
- [Crow] Ah, General Shawn.

1718
01:14:34,825 --> 01:14:36,325
Glad we found you.

1719
01:14:39,980 --> 01:14:41,537
- [Voiceover] Shawn.

1720
01:14:41,537 --> 01:14:42,370
Come on.

1721
01:14:42,370 --> 01:14:46,537
- [Servo] Come on, we have to
rescue our child that we hate.

1722
01:14:48,858 --> 01:14:51,941
- All homes of this area
must be evacuated at once.

1723
01:14:51,941 --> 01:14:52,982
- [Mike] The darlings.

1724
01:14:52,982 --> 01:14:55,574
You have no time to
remove your belongings.

1725
01:14:55,574 --> 01:14:56,947
Get out of the area.

1726
01:14:56,947 --> 01:14:59,781
Proceed in a westwardly direction.

1727
01:14:59,781 --> 01:15:02,527
- [Crow] Well the good
news is he may crush Sting.

1728
01:15:02,527 --> 01:15:03,360
- [Servo] You think so?

1729
01:15:03,360 --> 01:15:06,027
- [Mike] Good news for everyone.

1730
01:15:07,485 --> 01:15:09,177
- [Servo] A lot of people
will end up in hospital

1731
01:15:09,177 --> 01:15:10,094
because of this,

1732
01:15:10,094 --> 01:15:13,094
perhaps even people from university.

1733
01:15:24,204 --> 01:15:26,819
- [Crow] Oh not her majesty's
certified paper clip works,

1734
01:15:26,819 --> 01:15:30,986
purveyors of paper clip tour
majesty court since 1743.

1735
01:15:33,531 --> 01:15:37,614
- [Servo] It's the London
landmark Banco Espanol.

1736
01:15:40,476 --> 01:15:44,059
- [Mike] Hang on I
gotta change some pesos.

1737
01:15:47,279 --> 01:15:50,529
- [Crow] It's a Lulu autograph session.

1738
01:15:58,392 --> 01:16:00,224
- Run that way Sam.

1739
01:16:00,224 --> 01:16:01,127
We'll meet back at--

1740
01:16:01,127 --> 01:16:02,594
- [Mike] Great, about four?

1741
01:16:02,594 --> 01:16:04,344
I'll bring some beer.

1742
01:16:05,896 --> 01:16:08,229
(screaming)

1743
01:16:10,577 --> 01:16:14,102
- [Servo] What, what am I offending?

1744
01:16:14,102 --> 01:16:16,431
- [Mike] Maybe he just
hates Georgian architecture.

1745
01:16:16,431 --> 01:16:17,764
- [Servo] Maybe.

1746
01:16:18,799 --> 01:16:22,216
- [Crow] I hope that's not a mating call.

1747
01:16:26,285 --> 01:16:30,285
- [Servo] I'm glad you're
killing mother, Gorgo.

1748
01:16:32,569 --> 01:16:33,685
- [Mike] You need to find Elton John

1749
01:16:33,685 --> 01:16:35,532
so he can write a song about this.

1750
01:16:35,532 --> 01:16:37,750
♫ Goodbye England

1751
01:16:37,750 --> 01:16:41,917
♫ You've been crushed by giant lizards ♫

1752
01:16:43,903 --> 01:16:45,320
- [Crow] Big Ben.

1753
01:16:48,287 --> 01:16:52,454
- [Mike] Hey I'm just looking
for a good hat blocker.

1754
01:17:02,249 --> 01:17:06,010
I assume King Edward has
sold of all England's secrets

1755
01:17:06,010 --> 01:17:07,343
to Gorgo by now.

1756
01:17:11,992 --> 01:17:14,575
- [Servo] Man you are tub, kid.

1757
01:17:16,898 --> 01:17:19,171
- [Crow] I won't bury you.

1758
01:17:19,171 --> 01:17:21,004
- [Mike] Yes you will.

1759
01:17:24,378 --> 01:17:28,461
- [Servo] Come on my car's
gonna get towed, move.

1760
01:17:30,171 --> 01:17:31,004
- [Mike] At this point,

1761
01:17:31,004 --> 01:17:34,481
he's using the kid as a battering ram.

1762
01:17:34,481 --> 01:17:35,340
- [Servo] You know if it were me,

1763
01:17:35,340 --> 01:17:38,028
I'd just hang back and
kind of look inconspicuous.

1764
01:17:38,028 --> 01:17:39,620
- [Crow] Yeah, duck into a
corner, pull my hat down,

1765
01:17:39,620 --> 01:17:40,870
read the paper.

1766
01:17:49,247 --> 01:17:52,497
- [Mike] Aren't you glad you used Dial?

1767
01:17:53,363 --> 01:17:58,057
- [Servo] This guy panicked
but he stopped the path.

1768
01:17:58,057 --> 01:18:02,123
- [Mike] I'm looking
over a four leaf clover.

1769
01:18:02,123 --> 01:18:05,790
- [Crow] Stubby Kaye,
Al Lewis, Archie Rice.

1770
01:18:07,195 --> 01:18:09,511
- [Servo] Scabbed knees.

1771
01:18:09,511 --> 01:18:11,844
(screaming)

1772
01:18:19,350 --> 01:18:23,517
- [Mike] I trust event figure
will get me through this.

1773
01:18:28,142 --> 01:18:30,494
- [Servo] Insti-flood.

1774
01:18:30,494 --> 01:18:31,327
- It's alright Shawn.

1775
01:18:31,327 --> 01:18:33,393
We'll be alright.

1776
01:18:33,393 --> 01:18:35,560
- [Crow] It's Gorgo sweat.

1777
01:18:40,970 --> 01:18:43,044
- [Mike] Hey look, I
don't want to be near you.

1778
01:18:43,044 --> 01:18:45,461
Take me back to the soldiers.

1779
01:18:47,999 --> 01:18:52,166
- [Servo] By the way, does
this mean no work tomorrow?

1780
01:18:55,603 --> 01:18:57,470
- [Crow] Oh man, I floated
an air biscuit back there.

1781
01:18:57,470 --> 01:18:59,553
I gotta get away from it.

1782
01:19:01,357 --> 01:19:02,379
- Piccadilly, the heart of London.

1783
01:19:02,379 --> 01:19:04,236
Words can't describe it.

1784
01:19:04,236 --> 01:19:05,554
- [Mike] I'll speak in whole numbers.

1785
01:19:05,554 --> 01:19:07,181
- [Voiceover] Not even
the worst of a blitz.

1786
01:19:07,181 --> 01:19:09,116
This section is complete shambles.

1787
01:19:09,116 --> 01:19:11,066
People running mad with fear.

1788
01:19:11,066 --> 01:19:12,097
Fires everywhere.

1789
01:19:12,097 --> 01:19:16,723
- [Servo] The fire department
